    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20088" root="سقط" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِقَاطٌ</span></b>  <i>What falls from palm-trees, of unripe
dates:</i> (K:) or such are termed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِقَاطُ النَّخْلِ</span>:
(M:) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سقاط</span>, thus used, may be a sing., or pl. of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَاقِطٌ</span> [q. v.]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  (tropical:)  <i>Dates that are brought
from El-Yemámeh by those who journey thither
to procure them.</i> (M, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَقْطَةٌ</span>:
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَقَطٌ</span>, near the end of the paragraph: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4- 
and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِقْطٌ</span>, in two places, near the end of the
paragraph.

